  "query": "Explain the rules for building Houses and Hotels, including when they can be bought and any building limits.",
  "answer": "To build Houses and Hotels, you must first own all Sites of a color-group. You can buy Houses to put on any Site of that group, increasing the rent you may charge. The price is shown on the relevant Title Deed.\n\nHouses: You can buy them during your turn or between other players' turns but you must build evenly - one House per Site before building another. You cannot build a second House until all Sites have at least one House. Selling Houses works similarly, and you may do so as many times as your financial standing allows. However, if any Site of the same color-group is mortgaged, no Houses can be built.\n\nHotels: To buy a Hotel, you must first have four Houses on each Site of a complete color-group. Only one Hotel may be erected per Site. If there are no Houses left in the Bank, players must wait for others to return theirs before buying any. When selling Hotels, if none are available, they cannot be replaced with Houses.\n\nIn summary, you can buy or sell at any time and as many buildings as your financial standing allows, but building limits apply when a Site is mortgaged or no Houses are left in the Bank.",
